<title>ITALY: Italian bonds/futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian bonds/futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian bonds and futures ended quietly lower but had pared some losses by the close after surging last week on euphoria for Italy's maxi-budget for Europe. Traders said market was seen consolidating recent gains and for now good opportunities exist to buy on falls.</p>
<p>They noted Spanish bonos ended lower and bunds had also dipped after news U.S. September Chicago Purchasing Managers Index came in at 56.3 against a forecast 56.0 and August new home sales were higher than expected.</p>
<p>Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi welcomed results of the first Treasury auction since Friday's passage of the budget.</p>
</text>
